## <div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Sustainable Fashion – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 16px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

## <div style="margin-top: 20px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> Sustainable Fashion</td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> How History Is Fashionable</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Text: Summarize complex texts for peers. Communication: Resolve conflicts in group settings.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can summarize points from a fashion article by listing keywords (e.g., "eco-friendly" and "vintage" on a board as examples of trends).<br>Can resolve group disagreements on fashion ideas by guiding the discussion with simple language (e.g., "Can we choose one trend, like eco-fashion?" while showing a picture of eco-friendly materials).<br>Can explain fashion terms, using visuals and simple phrases in group discussions (e.g., "Sustainable means making choices that reduce environmental impact," while holding up eco-friendly fabric samples).</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>
</div>

## <h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px; text-align: center; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
        <thead>
            <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
                <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 30%; text-align: left;">Stage & Description</th>
                <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%; text-align: left;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
                <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 20%; text-align: left;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of fashion items from different historical periods (e.g., a flapper dress, 80s shoulder pads, a modern eco-friendly t-shirt). Students work in pairs to identify the decade or key trend and discuss what they notice about the materials or styles. The teacher asks: "How have fashion trends evolved from the past to today?" Students share their initial thoughts, focusing on general evolution and any examples of "vintage" or "retro" styles they've noticed. This also activates prior vocabulary from previous lessons.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to explain a fashion term or summarize a trend concisely. For example, pointing to an image of a 70s outfit, the teacher says: "In the 1970s, people were wearing wide flared jeans. It was a comfortable and stylish look, a retro trend that has returned." The teacher then points to a modern eco-friendly fabric sample and says: "This is a sustainable material. Sustainable means making choices that reduce environmental impact, like using recycled fabrics." The teacher emphasizes pronunciation of /v/ in "vintage" and /w/ in "wear," and stress in "sustainable."</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a fabric is 'sustainable,' does it harm the environment or help it?" (Expected answer: "Help it.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'in the 80s, people were wearing bright colors,' am I talking about one specific moment or a period of time?" (Expected answer: "A period of time.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</p>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short article (approx. 200 words) titled "From Past to Planet-Friendly: The Evolution of Sustainable Fashion." The article briefly describes how historical styles (e.g., repurposing clothes during wartime) laid groundwork for modern "sustainable" practices and how "brands" and "designers" are now creating "eco-friendly" "collections." It includes examples of "recycled materials" and "innovative" approaches. It also discusses "future" predictions for the "industry."</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Mediation: Text: Summarize complex texts for peers.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Reading:</b> Students read the article individually and identify the main idea: "What is the article mainly about?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Keyword Identification:</b> In small groups, students identify and list 5-7 keywords from the article related to fashion history and sustainability (e.g., "vintage," "eco-friendly," "recycled materials," "evolve," "prediction," "industry"). The teacher guides them to use the provided vocabulary list.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Sentence Completion:</b> Students complete sentences based on the text, using target grammar. E.g., "In the past, people ____ (adopt) clever ways to prolong clothing life. Today, brands ____ (showcase) their sustainable collections on the runway." "Before the 21st century, the focus ____ (be) less on eco-friendly materials." "Fashion trends ____ (continue) to evolve towards greater sustainability in the future."</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Past continuous with present simple to compare trends, Past perfect for completed actions, Future simple for predictions.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> (nouns) fashion, trend, vintage, retro, collection, style, materials, sustainability, launch, show, industry, brands, designs, runway, environment, prediction, history, personality, future; (verbs) evolve, predict, launch, adopt, reflect, discuss, shop, design, notice, gain, create, follow, introduce, showcase, wear, prefer, inspire, change, return, recycle; (adjectives) sustainable, fashionable, trendy, eco-friendly, vintage, retro, stylish, innovative, unique, recycled.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Practice /v/ in "vintage" and /w/ in "wear." Practice stress in "fashionable," "sustainability," "eco-friendly," "runway."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic:</b> Asking about fashion trends, discussing eco-friendly fashion choices.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                    <ol>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Keyword Summary:</b> In pairs, students take turns summarizing different sections of the article using the keywords they identified. Partner A reads a paragraph, then Partner B summarizes it using 2-3 keywords and a sentence structure like: "The paragraph explains that [keyword 1] is important because [details]. It also mentions [keyword 2] as a way to [details]." The teacher circulates, providing feedback on clarity and keyword usage. (e.g., "Eco-friendly materials were introduced to help the environment. They will be more common in the future.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Explaining Fashion Terms:</b> Students are given cards with fashion terms (e.g., "vintage," "sustainable," "fast fashion"). In new pairs, they must explain the term to their partner using simple language and examples, ensuring understanding. They use phrases like: "To clarify, 'vintage' refers to... Is that clear?" or "Basically, 'sustainable' means... Does that make sense?" Teacher prompts: "By using eco-friendly fabrics, fashion brands can reduce their carbon footprint, helping to protect the environment."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - Mediating a Trend Choice:</b> Each student is given a picture of a historical fashion trend (e.g., 90s grunge, 60s mod) and a modern sustainable trend (e.g., upcycling, vegan leather). In pairs, they must "mediate" a discussion to choose one trend for a hypothetical blog post, explaining their chosen trend and trying to convince their partner while also listening and summarizing their partner's points. They must use phrases for resolving disagreements: "I understand your point about [partner's trend], but can we choose one trend, like eco-fashion, that aligns with our theme?" "Perhaps we could find a compromise by including both, but focusing more on how [my trend] had adopted a sustainable approach?"</li>
                    </ol>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</p>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> "Fashion Trend Blog" Content Mediation Session.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">In groups of 3-4, students will work on developing a section for their "Fashion Trend Blog" (the 21st Century Skills Project). Each group member brings a different idea for a trend or a historical connection to sustainable fashion for the blog. They must collectively decide on the content for one section of their blog post. The main task is for students to mediate the discussion:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Explain Ideas:</b> Each student explains their proposed trend or concept for the blog, using descriptive language and linking it to the theme "How History Is Fashionable" and "Sustainable Fashion." (e.g., "I think we should discuss how in the 70s, people were wearing a lot of natural materials, and this reflected a growing awareness that will continue to evolve.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Summarize Contributions:</b> Students take turns summarizing their peers' ideas to ensure everyone understands. (e.g., "So, Juan, you're suggesting we include vintage denim because it's a recycled material that has always been fashionable, right?")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Resolve Conflicts:</b> If disagreements arise on which trends or historical points to include, students must use mediation strategies and polite language to guide the discussion towards a consensus. (e.g., "Some people say, 'fast fashion is cheap and convenient,' while others describe it as 'harmful and wasteful,' showing how language reflects different values about sustainability. Perhaps we can explain both perspectives in our blog?" or "We've had a lot of great ideas, but we need to finalize. Can we agree that in the last decades, people had adopted more casual fashion styles, which sometimes led to waste, but now the future will emphasize eco-friendly designs?")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Outline Creation:</b> The group must produce a brief, mediated outline for their blog section, incorporating the chosen trends and historical context, ready for writing.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher observes, offering support on language use for mediation and conflict resolution.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their mediated blog section outline to the class. One member (or rotated) explains one key trend, summarizing the historical context and its sustainable relevance, explaining any terms if needed. The teacher asks targeted questions to observe individual mediation skills.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation Checklist):</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity of Explanation/Summary:</b> Can the student summarize points from a fashion article/discussion clearly and concisely? (Mediation: Can summarize points from a fashion article by listing keywords...)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Appropriately uses nouns, verbs, and adjectives related to fashion and sustainability (e.g., "sustainable," "vintage," "evolve," "recycle").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Grammar:</b> Correctly uses past continuous with present simple, past perfect, and future simple to compare trends and make predictions. (e.g., "In the early 2000s, people were wearing low-rise jeans. Today, both flared and ripped jeans are in style.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Conflict Resolution Skills:</b> Guides group discussions with simple language to resolve disagreements. (Mediation: Can resolve group disagreements... by guiding the discussion with simple language.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Intelligible pronunciation of /v/ and /w/, and stress in multisyllabic words.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I was successful in mediating by __________ (e.g., summarizing my teammates' ideas, explaining a difficult term)."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One challenge I faced in explaining or summarizing was __________."</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What strategies did I use to explain difficult fashion terms or complex ideas (like 'sustainable industry') to my classmates today, and how effective were they?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did we manage to agree on our blog post ideas for the 'Fashion Trend Blog,' even with different opinions, and what role did I play in that process?"</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in promoting mediation skills (summarizing, explaining, conflict resolution)? Which activities effectively embedded the target grammar (past continuous, past perfect, future simple) and vocabulary in a mediation context?</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with summarizing complex texts or mediating group disagreements? How can we further develop their ability to discuss socio-linguistic aspects of fashion (e.g., different values regarding sustainability)?</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson served as a crucial step for planning the "Fashion Trend Blog." In the next session (or project phase), students will use their mediated outlines to draft the actual blog post, focusing on written expression and incorporating all the linguistic competences practiced in this unit.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                    <p style="margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>